18. The prospectus of First ICB Mutual Fund reveals &quot;the Fund is expected to continue without any limitation of time&quot;. The prospectus further reveals &quot;Distribution of profit in cash or kind depend upon the income&nbsp; and gains by such funds, and the prices of their certificates fluctuate with change in the supply of and demands for final certificates in&nbsp; the financial market&quot;. The prospectus also reveals&nbsp; &quot;The fund portfolio will be revolved&nbsp; from time to time for capital gains and for induction of new capital gains and for induction of new securities promising growth&nbsp; and attractive yields&quot;.&nbsp;&nbsp; 

 28. The latest amendment to the Rules permits extension of the period by the unit holders and if that is so then the so-called limitation as to the period and the amount of the fund is no longer there. In fact, there was no restriction before the impugned amendment in law on the power of the trustees to change the nature of the fund by increasing its period or the capital. A fund is a trust and not a statutory creation. Its nature has been mentioned in the Rules and it is for the beneficiaries and the trustees to amend the terms of the trust subject, of course, to the requirement that such change will ensure to the benefit of the trustees and the beneficiaries.&nbsp; 

 29. Increase of capital of the fund and issuance of bonus share (stock dividend) were permitted by the Securities and Exchange Commission although such practice goes against the definition of closed-end fund which is a fund which specifies the period and&nbsp; the capital. SEC having permitted payment of stock dividend itself now estopped from retracting from it. The life span of all the 8 ICB Mutual Funds does not have any limitation and therefore, there has been no extension of their life span. According to the prospectus of 1st BSRS Mutual Fund, this has no limitation of life either. The period of AIMS 1st Mutual Fund was extended in 2005 up to 2015.&nbsp;
